Nothing excludes or restricts a liability, legal guarantee, remedy or
mandatory protection that cannot lawfully be excluded or restricted.
No zero liability cap is inferred from the fact that software rights
are royalty-free. A separately agreed service obligation is not
silently cancelled by this software-license disclaimer.

12. Duration, breach and termination

The copyright permissions granted here have the duration stated in section
2, subject to termination for breach, not discretionary retrospective
withdrawal of compliant recipients' rights. For a remediable breach,
Licensor must notify the affected person of the breach, the required
remedy and a reasonable remediation period appropriate to the
circumstances before terminating those permissions for failure to cure.

For serious or repeated violations, notice and remedies must address
their gravity and recurrence. Immediate cessation of the infringing
activity and other proportionate measures available under applicable
law may be sought; this does not silently remove the reasonable-cure
protection for remediable breaches. An irremediable breach may lead to
termination by reasoned notice, subject to applicable law. This text
does not create an automatic restoration mechanism following termination.

Termination of one person's rights does not by itself terminate rights
of downstream recipients who comply with their own applicable terms,
nor rights independently held under third-party licenses or law.
Attribution and source obligations already incurred remain due to the
extent permitted by law. No provision authorizes remote deletion,
erasure of user data, alteration of credentials or any automatic data
destruction mechanism. Cessation of unauthorized acts is distinct from
destruction of users' information.

13. French law, jurisdiction, language and earlier rights

French law governs this license, subject to mandatory rules
and protections that cannot be waived, including applicable consumer
protections. Jurisdiction is determined by the applicable rules; no
exclusive court displacing those rules is imposed here.

The English version is authoritative. A French translation is
supplied for information; this language rule does not
override mandatory information or language requirements.

Neither adoption of new terms nor replacement of a repository file
purports to revoke permissions validly obtained under an earlier
license, override mandatory rights, or alter third-party licenses.
No automatic election of any later license version is introduced.

